    "body": "Fixes #8122.\n\nSince 3.2.0, `a, b = s[i:]` crashes the compiler with `AssertionError: <NOT CONSTANT>` when the slice start is not a compile-time constant. `SliceIndexNode.inferable_item_node()` passes `not_a_constant` on as the index in that case, and `ExprNode.inferable_item_node()` hands it to `IntNode.for_size()`, which only accepts an `int` since a2a713e (GH-7018). For `not_a_constant` it now builds the `IntNode` the way it did before that change, so type inference sees an index with an unknown value, as in 3.1.x.\n\nI added tests to `tests/run/unpack.pyx` for a non-constant start, a non-constant start and stop, a typed `list` argument, a `tuple[int, str, float]` argument and starred targets. They fail to compile on master and pass with the change.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/cython/cython/pull/8151#discussion_r4657210231"
